#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ccdeck: a live dashboard for your local Claude Code sessions.

A terminal list and a live dashboard (http://localhost:7799) for every Claude
Code session on this machine: which are open, which need you, which have a PR
waiting for review, and which are done. Python 3.9+ standard library only;
`gh` (GitHub CLI) is used for PR states when installed.

    ccdeck                 sessions grouped by what they need
    ccdeck -a              include done and old sessions
    ccdeck show ID         details: PRs, links, files, last message
    ccdeck done ID [NOTE]  mark solved          (undone ID to reopen)
    ccdeck park ID         set aside for later   (unpark ID)
    ccdeck note ID TEXT    attach your own note
    ccdeck resume ID       cd to the session's folder and `claude --resume`
    ccdeck serve           run the dashboard in the foreground
    ccdeck open            open the dashboard in the browser
    ccdeck install         hooks + background service + app launcher
    ccdeck uninstall       remove all of that again

ID is a row number from the last list or any unique prefix of a session id.
"""

